Currently a ring of conflict is a pretty powerful item that doesn't seem
to have any adverse side effects (other than endangering your pet around
powerful monsters).  I think the game would be more interesting if
the effects of the ring were enhanced:

A cursed ring of conflict should just give you aggravate monster.
Perhaps it should increase the damage monsters do to you -- "the
maddened orc hits, the maddened killer bee hits".

An uncursed ring of conflict should make monsters randomly attack an
adjacent monster -- which might include you!  This would make it
effective, but also make it a little more even; you wouldn't be able to
just walk up to a master lich or black dragon and pound away with no
fear.  You would still have to take a wide berth around rust monsters,
ochre jellies, etc.  They could also still do extra damage from
"madness".

A blessed ring of conflict should work like the current ring does.  This
would force you to at least use up a potion of holy water to get the
full benefit.

Is it my imagination, or do monsters with defensive attacks not do them
against attacks by pets or due to other conflict?  I notice how easily a
kitten can deal with acid blobs, blue jellies, even ochre jellies
(although I think my pet was a housecat by then).

Along the same lines, do monsters that swallow do proportionally more
damage when in conflict with other monsters?  I've seen purple worms
especially kill some powerful opponents in a single turn.  Anyone ever
polymorph into a purple worm to find out if you can swallow critters
with #monster?

